"I See You"
In a house where silence screams,  
You hide your hurt behind soft dreams.  
A mother’s words, too sharp, too cold,  
Leave your young heart feeling old.

You speak, but no one hears you out,  
Your voice gets lost in fear and doubt.  
Still, ypou smile and carry on,  
Like sunlight breaking through the dawn.

I see the tears you never show,  
The strength it takes to quietly grow.  
You love so deep, though love feels thin,  
Still hoping someone lets you in.

You’re not the fault, you’re not the pain,  
You’re not the thunder, nor the rain.  
You are the calm, the quiet grace,  
The strength behind a weary face.

So when the world won’t let you be,  
Come rest your voice, your soul, with me.  
I’ll listen gently, hold your light,  
And remind you—you'll be all right.
